  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "First release: Microsoft sign-in for work and school accounts through the server-side authorization code flow with PKCE, a browser-bound encrypted state, ID token validation against Microsoft's signing keys, tenant rules, and per-request max authentication age and Conditional Access authentication context checks, with the sign-in endpoints POST /api/auth/microsoft/begin and POST /api/auth/microsoft reporting every attempt to the audit logger. An app's own flows also get the validated raw ID token on the completion result, as signing evidence to seal with a record and never log. Requires EasyReasy.Auth 5.14.0. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/easy-reasy/blob/auth-microsoft-v1.0.0/EasyReasy.Auth.Microsoft/README.md",
